  "releaseNotes": "When using this version for building register layouts, you must also use a Triamec.Tools.Registers NuGet >= 8.0.0.\n\n      New:\n      - The TAM configuration now stores the date and time when the file was created.\n      - Added support for Firmware 5 (Register Layout 20)\n      - TamAxis.MoveAbsolute now have overloads allowing to start a snap-constrained move. A new parameter allows to specify nth-order motion. At the time of writing, this feature cannot be combined with modulo mo­ves.\n      - Acquisitions: new extension methods IVariable.Duration() and IVariable.SubsequentTime() to ease computation with timestamps.\n      - New programming model to load, link and dismiss Tama programs and to control their tasks and state. Refer to PCN017 for more information.\n\n      Bug:\n      - Fixed a NullReferenceException crash when opening a TAMdmp file.\n      - Improved shutdown behavior in the Ethernet connection such that no UnobservedTaskExceptions occur anymore on .NET Core.\n      \n      Deprecated:\n      - ITamDevice.TamaManager is deprecated. Use ITamDevice.Programs instead.\n\n      Security:\n      - Update transitive dependency System.Security.Cryptography.Xml from 7.0.1 to 8.0.4 (fixes CVE-2021-24112, CVE-2024-38095, CVE-2023-29331, CVE-2019-0820)\n      - Updated transitive dependency System.Security.Cryptography.Xml from 8.0.4 to 10.0.14 (fixes CVE-2026-84008, CVE-2026-70162, CVE-2026-96222, CVE-2026-96958, CVE-2026-96959, CVE-2026-96960)",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
